%% IICPC end-to-end benchmark pipeline — one run, from user click to score.
%% Technical view: every Kafka message carries its key, encoding, and acks, the
%% measurement spine (eBPF capture to telemetry to validator) is shown inline.
%% High-level "what lives where" is in k8s_namespaces.mermaid.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    participant U as User
    participant API as submission-api<br/>Go · platform ns
    participant K as Kafka (KRaft)<br/>data ns · RF=3 · minISR=2
    participant CTL as bot-fleet-controller<br/>Go · benchmark ns · 1 replica
    participant ORCH as sandbox-orchestrator<br/>Go · sandbox ns
    participant ALGO as algo-{session}<br/>contestant Pod · gVisor · sandbox ns
    participant CAP as ebpf-latency capture<br/>Rust · 1 Job per slot
    participant W as bot-fleet workers<br/>Rust · KEDA 2..50 · benchmark ns
    participant TI as telemetry-ingester<br/>Rust · benchmark ns
    participant CV as correctness-validator<br/>Go · benchmark ns

    Note over U,CV: PRECONDITION submissions.status == 'ready' — image already built (Kaniko), scanned (Trivy/Syft),<br/>and promoted to Harbor production by build-worker. Postgres status is the trust anchor (no image signing).

    rect rgba(250,240,220,0.4)
        Note over U,API: Trigger
        U->>API: POST /benchmarks/{submission_id}
        Note over API: session_id = UUIDv7 (embedded ms timestamp, k-sortable)<br/>idempotency: partial unique index run_groups(submission_id) WHERE status NOT IN (completed,failed)<br/>re-trigger of an active group returns it with HTTP 200, never a duplicate run
        API->>K: benchmark.requested (one per scenario)<br/>key=session_id · JSON · acks=all
        API-->>U: 202 { run_group_id }
    end

    rect rgba(220,240,220,0.4)
        Note over CTL,CAP: Sandbox slot provisioning + measurement attach (HTTP + k8s API, not Kafka)
        K->>CTL: deliver benchmark.requested (group bot-fleet-controller) — sessions run SERIALLY
        CTL->>ORCH: POST /slots { slot_id=session_id, image, port∈{8080,9898} }
        Note over ORCH: reject non-capturable port (HTTP 400) so a run can't silently evade measurement
        ORCH->>ALGO: k8s API: create Pod + Service<br/>Guaranteed QoS (integer CPU = exclusive cpuset) · readOnlyRootFS + 4 tmpfs<br/>drop ALL caps · seccomp RuntimeDefault · no SA token · activeDeadline 3600s
        ORCH->>CAP: k8s API: create capture Job (hostPID, CAP_BPF/NET_ADMIN)<br/>ownerRef=algo Pod · TTL 300s · Burstable (never steals the pinned cores)
        CAP->>ALGO: enter algo netns: ethtool -K eth0 tso/gso/gro/lro off (one packet = one order)<br/>attach XDP ingress (t3) + tc-clsact egress (t7)
        loop poll 500ms · deadline 60s
            CTL->>ORCH: GET /slots/{session_id}
            ORCH-->>CTL: { state: creating|ready|failed, endpoint }
        end
    end

    rect rgba(220,220,250,0.5)
        Note over CTL,W: Workload dispatch — the bot-fleet contract
        Note over CTL: worker_count = ceil(total_tasks / 1000)<br/>shard task list round-robin by task_id (each pod gets a representative profile mix)
        CTL->>K: N × WorkloadSpec<br/>topic workload.assignments · key=session_id:worker_index · JSON · acks=all
        K->>W: deliver WorkloadSpec (group bot-fleet)
        Note over W: connect all sockets + FIX logon at barrier time (cold-start isolated)<br/>precompute every order frame in RAM, seeded RNG = global_seed XOR task_id (byte-identical replay)<br/>TCP_NODELAY on all transports
        W->>ALGO: TCP connect × bot_count
        W->>K: ReadySignal · topic bot.ready · key=session_id:worker_id · acks=all (control plane)
        K->>CTL: deliver bot.ready × N (group bot-fleet-controller-ready)
        Note over CTL: fan-in until count == worker_count (deadline 30s, partial = degraded)
    end

    rect rgba(250,220,220,0.5)
        Note over CTL,W: Barrier — atomic simultaneous fire (no PTP)
        CTL->>K: BarrierEvent · key=session_id · acks=all<br/>target_epoch = now + 500ms safety gap (computed AFTER fan-in, never stale-in-the-past)
        Note over W: every worker reads the same barrier offset via its own consumer group
        K->>W: BarrierEvent
        Note over W: sleep_until(local Instant derived from absolute epoch) — all bots unblock within Kafka jitter
    end

    rect rgba(240,240,220,0.5)
        Note over W,CAP: Hot path — fixed-interval pacing (coordinated-omission correct)
        loop per task at fixed interval (next_send never recoils by work duration)
            Note over W: t0 = next_send_ns (intended, pre-sleep), sleep_until, write frame, t1 = clock (post-write).<br/>read path takes first ExecutionReport per ClOrdID as r9, watchdog evicts at 5s with timed_out=true
            W->>ALGO: FIX / REST / WS order frame (O(1) in-place tag52 + checksum-delta patch)
            ALGO-->>W: ExecutionReport (FIX response path)
        end
        ALGO->>CAP: every request/response packet copied by the kernel hooks
        Note over CAP: userspace TCP reassembly (coalescing + straddling, first-byte timestamp),<br/>parse FIX/HTTP/WS, match response to request by ClOrdID,<br/>one OrderAckedEvent per ACK and per partial fill (shares the request's t3)
        W->>K: orders.sent (MessagePack named, batched <=1000/msg, acks=1) · key=session_id
        CAP->>K: orders.acked (MessagePack named, chunked <=1000/msg, drains only what Kafka accepted)
    end

    rect rgba(225,235,245,0.5)
        Note over K,TI: Live metrics (during the run)
        K->>TI: orders.sent + orders.acked (group telemetry-ingester)
        Note over TI: join on order_id (bounded, 5s idle evict) to HDR histograms per (session, contestant, wave)<br/>service_time = t7−t3 (scored) · response_time = r9−t0 (CO signal) · schedule_slip = t1−t0<br/>wave_index = floor((t0−session_start)/wave) — pure time bucket, no scenario lookup
        TI->>K: (writes) metrics hypertable (TimescaleDB) + hot p99 (Redis) every 1s
    end

    rect rgba(220,240,240,0.4)
        Note over CTL,CV: Completion + post-run scoring
        CTL->>ORCH: DELETE /slots/{session_id} (algo Pod + Service torn down, capture Job GC'd via ownerRef/TTL)
        CTL->>K: benchmark.status.updated { status: completed } · key=session_id · acks=all
        K->>API: deliver status (group submission-api-benchmark-status) to UPDATE runs, release the unique index
        K->>CV: status==completed triggers validation (group correctness-validator)
        Note over CV: bounded drain (UUIDv7 session-start window) to replay in TCP-HOL-aware effective_t3 order<br/> to reference price-time-priority order book to 6 violation classes to scores.correctness<br/>idempotent: one worker claims via INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING, only the claimer publishes
        CV->>K: scores.correctness · key=session_id · JSON
    end

    Note over U,CV: Scoring layer (built): score-computer consumes scores.correctness + per-wave metrics (TimescaleDB)<br/> to peak-sustained-TPS = highest wave passing median-p99≤1ms + error≤1% + coverage≥90%, skipping warmup wave 0<br/> to correctness DQ if valid/total < 0.95 (per-session or aggregate) to scores table<br/> to leaderboard-api (2s Redis cache on list) + SSE to frontend.
